Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:11:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-n56: Enable the display pipe

The iPhone 6 Plus's display pipe and display DART are the iPod touch 6's.
Read from its Apple device tree (iOS 12.4, 16G77, n56ap), disp0 is
"adbe0,t7000" with the same windows, interrupts (103, 108-111), power
gate (112) and clock gates (112, 118, 116); dart-disp0 has the same
windows, interrupts (106, 107), error reflector (0x20ffff000), fetch and
diag configuration and gate (36); and the panel link is the same
two-lane mipi-dsim (0x206600000, gate 113) with an "lcd,pinot" panel
whose supply is on the display PMU. So t7000.dtsi's description holds,
and disp0 only needs enabling. dart-disp0 stays disabled: the display
driver enables it after mapping the live scanout.

What differs from the iPod touch 6, read from the ADT: two LM3534
backlight controllers, a display EEPROM (i2c2, 0x51), and a SAC range
and divisor (0x38) on mipi-dsim. None of them is touched by the display
pipe's driver. The ADT has no panel timing; the 1080x1920 mode is
inferred from the iPhone 6 Plus's panel, and the driver takes the real
one from the boot framebuffer. This is the largest framebuffer the A8's
pipe adopts (8.3 MB at 32 bpp), and the display DART self-check's
pattern is sized from it.

Not run on an iPhone 6 Plus yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n56.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n56.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n56.dts
index 2c358df..beab275 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n56.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n56.dts
@@ -12,3 +12,11 @@
 	compatible = "apple,n56", "apple,t7000", "apple,arm-platform";
 	model = "Apple iPhone 6 Plus";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The display pipe takes the 1080x1920 MIPI DSI panel over from simpledrm.
+ * No panel supply is given: the panel stays on in system sleep.
+ */
+&disp0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
